{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "997f6e2e-18f7-8139-9c0a-57f666722cb4",
  "created_at": "2026-03-06T11:16:40-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, City Clerk",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Fatima Furtado",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sandra Pimentel",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:14:21-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Clerk's office, this is Sandra. Good morning, how can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:14:26-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning. Yes, hello. Um, I am calling about old records. Genealogy, I think is the word? For my family, from the nineteen thirties."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:14:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh sure, we get those. Are you looking for a birth, a marriage, or a death record?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:14:40-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Birth, I think. My husband's grandmother. She was born here in Newport, maybe nineteen thirty-four. Or thirty-five, I am not sure. Is this the same, genealogy and the regular certificate?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:14:50-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not exactly the same, no. Older records are handled a little differently than recent ones, and who can request them depends on the relationship. You said your husband's grandmother, so you'd be a couple of steps removed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:02-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, okay. So I am not the, how you say, direct family? I am the wife of the grandson."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:08-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, so it may be easier if your husband comes in or signs something. But for a record that old, there may be more flexibility. Let me make sure I tell you right. Do you have her full name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:20-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. But the spelling, it can be two ways. I have to check with him. Can I ask first, what ID I bring? My license, is it enough?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:29-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A photo ID like your driver's license is what you'd bring. And if you're asking on behalf of someone, something showing the family connection helps. Like your marriage certificate, or your husband's birth certificate."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So two papers. My license, and then the paper for the marriage. And his birth paper also? Or one or the other?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:47-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Either one that shows how you're connected. If you bring both, even better. Better to have too much than too little."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:15:54-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. I write this down. Sorry, my phone, I am looking for pen. [pause] Oh, wait. I have the sticky note on the wall, with the number I called. I wrote it there from the website. So now I write on it the ID things."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:16:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a good place for it. Keep that number handy. If you want to check anything before you come down, just call us."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:16:15-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I will. And the office, you are open today? Because it is raining, I think I wait for after."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:16:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We're here till four-thirty today, but I don't blame you, it's supposed to be wet all day. Come when it's nicer."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:16:29-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Sandra. I am still a little confused with who can ask, but I ask my husband and I come."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T11:16:36-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, we'll sort it out at the counter. Take care now."
    }
  ],
